# Allowlist for the Trivy image scan in .github/workflows/deploy-ec2.yml.
#
# One CVE (or GHSA) ID per line, alone on the line; put the justification in a
# comment on the line(s) above it. An entry suppresses the finding entirely,
# including from the SARIF upload to code scanning — so every entry MUST carry
# a comment explaining why it is accepted and, where possible, a link to the
# upstream issue or advisory. An unexplained entry is a silent hole in the
# release gate.
#
# Legitimate reasons look like:
#   - a Debian "won't fix" / negligible CVE in the node:22-bookworm-slim base
#     that upstream declines to patch
#   - a fix exists but only in a package the runtime genuinely cannot drop or
#     bump yet, with the reason recorded
#
# The scan already passes ignore-unfixed, so "no fix published yet" alone is
# NOT a reason for an entry — those are filtered automatically.
#
# Example entry:
#   # CVE-2024-12345 — in libfoo, marked wont-fix by Debian; the server never
#   # reaches that code path. https://security-tracker.debian.org/...
#   CVE-2024-12345
#
# There are no ignored vulnerabilities today; the file exists so the workflow
# and contributors have a documented place for them.
